# EKS Infrastructure – Allegro Project

## ⚠️ NOTE: S3 Backend Configuration
This project uses a remote state stored in S3 with a lock in DynamoDB.

### Infrastructure parameters:
- **Region:** `eu-north-1`
- **Bucket Name:** `allegro-analytics-eks-tfstate-2026`
- **DynamoDB Table:** `terraform-state-lock`
- **Secrets Manager** `allegro-app-secrets-dev` for development and `allegro-app-secrets-prod` for production

### Synchronization instructions:
The same bucket name **MUST** appear in two places:
1. `.bootstrap/variables.tf` -> variable `state_bucket_name`
2. `./backend.tf` -> the `bucket` parameter in the `backend “s3”` block

---

## Setup steps:
### 1. Go to `.bootstrap/` and run `terraform apply`.
### 2. Go to  `envs/dev/` and run `terraform apply`.
### 3. Go to AWS and SSM into mgmt-asg EC2 and configure it:
 
```
### 5. After running Cilium - Delete AWS VPC CNI. Next restart DNS and ArgoCD (critical for refresh config)
kubectl delete ds aws-node -n kube-system
kubectl delete ds kube-proxy -n kube-system
kubectl rollout restart deployment coredns -n kube-system
k rollout restart -n external-secrets deployment


git clone -b testing https://github.com/Rehox0/allegro-analytics-eks.git
kubectl apply -f ~/allegro-analytics-eks/k8s/gitops/root/root-app.yaml

k rollout restart -n argocd deployment
k rollout restart -n argocd statefulset



#ArgoCD UI
On mgmt:
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443

##ArgoCD UI
<!-- Locally run: -->
aws ssm start-session \
  --target i-xxxxxxxxxxxxxx \
  --document-name AWS-StartPortForwardingSession \
  --parameters '{"portNumber":["8080"],"localPortNumber":["8080"]}'


kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d


```
